SUMMARY:Zeta Values as Moments: A Random Matrix Theory
DESCRIPTION:The values of the Riemann zeta-function $\\zeta\\left(\\alpha+\\beta n\\right)$ with $\\alpha>1$\, $\\beta>0$ and $n$ a positive integer can be viewed as moments of a probability distribution. In my talk I will construct the corresponding random matrix model and determine its asymptotic spectral curve\, which exhibits an unusual feature\, the complete asymptotics of its partition function and uniform approx\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/17408/
LOCATION:IHES
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/17408/
