SUMMARY:On the Wilson-Fisher Fixed Point in the Limit of Integer Spacetime Dimensions
DESCRIPTION:The Wilson–Fisher (WF) fixed point\, a scalar field theory with a quartic interaction in $d = 4 - \\epsilon$ dimensions\, is the textbook example of a weakly coupled CFT. The epsilon expansion accurately reproduces the critical exponents of the $d = 3$ and the $d = 2$ Ising model. This has led to the common view that WF defines a continuous family of CFTs in non-integer dimensions\, interpolating betw\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/17103/
LOCATION:IHES
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/17103/
END:VEVENT
